{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T08:45:02.256Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-g2zzus","claim:pm-gh1769","claim:pm-lulgxc","lineage:pm-g2zzus","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-g2zzus+pm-gh1769+pm-lulgxc","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-g2zzus","claim:pm-gh1769","claim:pm-lulgxc","lineage:pm-g2zzus","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-dhlij3"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"An installed extension whose registerItemFields names a reserved item key makes every pm create and pm update fail with untyped command_failed, and package doctor does not name the cause"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Measured 2026-11-23 on the 2026.11.23 build while closing pm-3s4jwl. A project extension that calls api.registerItemFields([{ name: 'priority', type: 'string' }]) activates without a refusal. Afterwards every pm create (with or without --field) and every pm update (pm update <id> --title t2) exits 2 with code command_failed and the detail 'Extension item field \"priority\" collides with built-in item metadata \"priority\"; rename the extension field...'. Reads keep working (pm list returns items). pm package doctor reports only extension_custom_field_mcp_input_collision for the field, and pm health --check-only says nothing about it, so the operator sees a tracker whose writes all fail with an untyped code and no diagnostic that names the package. pm-ghf1 (closed) added the reserved-key check to SDK lint, preflight and the test harness, so a package author is warned, but an already published or hand-written package still disables all writes for every user of the tracker. Duplicate check: searched 'extension item field collides with built-in item metadata reserved create fails'; pm-ghf1 owns authoring-time detection only, pm-3s4jwl owns built-in option collisions."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","extensions","schema","ux"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-23T08:45:02.256Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T08:45:02.256Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Activation refuses only the reserved field registration with a typed code that names the package, the field and the reserved key, and pm create and pm update keep working for every other field; pm package doctor and pm health report the refused registration with the package name and a rename hint; A regression spec installs such an extension and drives create and update on the built CLI, with a negative control showing the pre-fix refusal"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"One package's reserved field name cannot disable writes for the whole tracker; the refusal is typed and diagnosable"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Every create and update exits 2 with command_failed while the extension is active; doctor names only the MCP input collision"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-3s4jwl","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-23T08:45:02.256Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-ghf1","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-23T08:45:02.256Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a6ce89a73bfb976188f87c402fa084d0966fea79619f398bd05f6650c805d464","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"1ad9452e23ef6b5a867b665e10e16c6e9439dc03ab589515a1cfcb03c918a671"}
