{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T03:31:48.251Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6a627c6a9d6772d54597ee42","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2nwcgg","claim:pm-dhlij3","claim:pm-x9r2h3","lineage:pm-2nwcgg","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-2nwcgg+pm-dhlij3+pm-x9r2h3","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2nwcgg","claim:pm-dhlij3","claim:pm-x9r2h3","lineage:pm-2nwcgg","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T03:31:48.251Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-27T03:31:48.250Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Root cause and fix (2026-11-27, branch fix/field-admission-diagnostics). Two defects combined: (1) the loader accepted a registerItemFields definition named after built-in item metadata, and every write then ran applyRegisteredItemFieldDefaultsAndValidation, which refuses the reserved name; (2) create.ts and update.ts wrapped that call in a catch that rebuilt every error as a plain PmCliError, so the typed extension_item_field_reserved code (and extension_item_field_type_conflict) surfaced as command_failed. Fix: ExtensionApiRegistrar.registerItemFields drops only the reserved field and pushes the activation warning extension_item_field_reserved:<layer>:<package>:<field>:rename=<prefix>_<field> (formatReservedItemFieldWarning in src/core/extensions/item-fields.ts); a registration that held only reserved fields registers nothing. Both write paths now call applyRegisteredItemFieldDefaultsForWrite, which rethrows a PmCliError unchanged and turns the validation TypeErrors into usage refusals. Activation warnings already reach package doctor and health, so both now name the package, field and rename; the MCP input collision row for the dropped field disappears with it. Evidence on the built CLI in a sandbox tracker: create --field review_owner=ada exits 0, update --title exits 0, doctor and health list the warning; tests/unit/extensions/extension-item-field-admission.spec.ts (5 cases) covers activation, the write path (a hand-built registry is the negative control that still reaches the write path), and the built CLI. Negative control: with src reverted to main, all 5 cases fail."}]}],"before_hash":"19fd44101786fe69b0d7a8712c2eab388440fcd5194b25bb744fb3cdffc02a0f","after_hash":"45b2d65221b71d58298b2fbd6cf5a673a71de3196612c3d958f7971644e6abd7","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d7782020bff5d013429d726f55997dfa9e1b7183b9f21da6ad503909dfe0cf90"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T04:02:40.566Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6a627c6a9d6772d54597ee42","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2nwcgg","claim:pm-dhlij3","claim:pm-x9r2h3","lineage:pm-2nwcgg","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-2nwcgg+pm-dhlij3+pm-x9r2h3","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-2nwcgg","claim:pm-dhlij3","claim:pm-x9r2h3","lineage:pm-2nwcgg","lineage:pm-ugqx","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-27T04:02:40.566Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Correction to the fix note above (2026-11-27): a registerItemFields call whose fields are all reserved now keeps an empty registration entry instead of registering nothing. The package did register against the schema capability, so the harness least-privilege check (assertExtensionCapabilityUsage) and capability usage stay truthful; registration_counts.item_fields counts fields, so it still reports 0 for that call. Test fixtures in sdk-index.spec.ts and extension-loader.spec.ts that asserted registered fields named severity and risk (both reserved item keys, so those fields already broke every write) now use incident_severity and risk_score. The write-path helper is imported directly from core/extensions/item-fields.js so it does not join the public ./sdk surface."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T04:02:40.566Z"}],"before_hash":"45b2d65221b71d58298b2fbd6cf5a673a71de3196612c3d958f7971644e6abd7","after_hash":"6eb8256b19f68ae0cae85903fa0739e68381a5bfc1500714becc5f2476ad6b3b","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4f9cc7057bfd2cbc094e18b99778ad3201f4a68e033d423ec05aae3637f63102"}
